# Git pull -- not on the push host (mandatory)

[git-per-host-clone.mdc](git-per-host-clone.mdc) and [cluster-sync-order.mdc](cluster-sync-order.mdc) Phase C:

| Host role in this change | `git pull --ff-only`? |
|--------------------------|------------------------|
| **Same machine** where the agent (or operator) just **`git commit` + `git push`** | **No** -- checkout is already at `origin/main`. |
| **Every other clone** that will deploy or run scripts from that repo | **Yes** -- before deploy on that host. |

## Forbidden in agent replies

- "Pull on `orchestrator`" immediately after pushing alfa-ai from `orchestrator` / `C:\Users\operator\alfa-ai`.
- Generic "pull then start" when the only consumer of the change **is** the push host (e.g. Trainer GUI Start on `orchestrator` after pushing `Start-AlfaTrain7bQlora.ps1`).
- Listing the push host in a Phase C pull table for the same commit the agent just pushed.

## Required handoff after push from active workspace

1. Confirm **commit is on the push host** (e.g. `fc4224d5` already local after successful push).
2. Tell the operator the **next action on that host** (open GUI, run script, orchestrator) with **no pull**.
3. If other hosts need parity, list **only those hosts** with one pull step each (`hub` operator,
   `inference`, `apps`, `C:\alfa-ai-train` on `gaming_c`/`gaming_b` when *they* must run updated code).

## Self-check before Send

```
Did I push (or did the operator push) from this host in this thread?
  yes -> do not post git pull for that host
  no  -> pull only on consumers named in the runbook
```

## Example (this mistake class)

**Wrong:** Push from `orchestrator`, then "From `orchestrator`: `git pull --ff-only origin main`" before GUI Start.

**Right:** Push from `orchestrator`, then "Trainer GUI Start on `orchestrator` -- no pull; clone is already current."

